{"retryCount is updated as reminder.retryCount + 1 using a value read earlier via findMany, so concurrent scheduler runs can overwrite each other and lose increments, making the two failures then delete behavior unreliable": 0.7994539737701416, "scheduleSMSReminders deletes any WorkflowReminder with retryCount > 1 because the deleteMany uses a top-level OR where the retryCount branch is not scoped to SMS, which can delete non-SMS reminders (EMAIL/WHATSAPP) if their retryCount is ever incremented": 0.9562023282051086, "When twilioProvider.scheduleSMS returns undefined due to SMS sending being locked, scheduleSMSReminders treats it as a scheduling failure and increments retryCount, causing reminders to be deleted after two cron runs even though they were skipped intentionally due to a lock": 0.8884157538414001}